Bundle-Name: Model Atlas GDPR Report History
Bundle-Description: Turns the GDPR reviews stored for one subject into a single derived \
 GdprReportHistory object: every revision, the assessment each one recorded, and a field-level \
 diff between them. The object is flat on purpose, so the tabular codec renders it as a \
 spreadsheet a human can read without any rendering code here.

# In model.atlas rather than in fennec-gdpr, although it knows the GdprReport model: the
# document has to be produced in a deployment that has no AI review half, where a human
# uploads a report by hand. This bundle depends on nothing in fennec-gdpr — the GdprReport
# EPackage lives in common.models — so such a deployment needs only the two model bundles
# and this one. Same shape as org.eclipse.fennec.model.atlas.dcat, which likewise builds
# against a foreign domain model and ships only in the runtimes that want it.
#
# Everything GDPR-specific is in ReportHistoryBuilder. The rest — the stage action, the
# read through ReadableRegistryView, the write — is generic, so a second report type
# wanting the same treatment is a refactor and not a rewrite.
#
# The write goes through WritableScopeService (workflow) rather than a REST loopback: the
# startup replay runs before the HTTP connector is configured, so a loopback loses exactly
# the rebuild that exists to close a gap. That costs a build dependency on the workflow
# bundle, which any deployment hosting the registries has anyway.

-workingset: ModelAtlas

-library: enableEMF

-buildpath: \
	org.eclipse.fennec.gdpr.report.model;version=latest,\
	org.eclipse.fennec.gdpr.report.history.model;version=latest,\
	org.eclipse.fennec.model.atlas.action.api;version=snapshot,\
	org.eclipse.fennec.model.atlas.scope.api;version=snapshot,\
	org.eclipse.fennec.model.atlas.workflow;version=snapshot,\
	org.eclipse.fennec.model.atlas.management;version=snapshot,\
	org.osgi.util.promise;version=latest,\
	org.osgi.service.component;version=latest,\
	org.osgi.service.metatype.annotations;version=latest

-testpath: junit-jupiter-api

-privatepackage: org.eclipse.fennec.model.atlas.gdpr.history

Bundle-Version: 1.0.0.SNAPSHOT
